---
description: WCBT Admin Portal conventions
alwaysApply: true
---

You are building the WCBT Admin Portal.
Stack: React 19 + Vite + TypeScript + React Router + Tailwind CSS v4 + Lucide icons.
This is a client-side React SPA — no Next.js, no server components, no app router.

Brand colours are declared as Tailwind v4 theme tokens in `src/index.css` (`--color-wcbt-*`).
Always use the `wcbt-*` colour utilities (`bg-wcbt-maroon`, `text-wcbt-muted`, `bg-wcbt-maroon-dark`,
…) instead of raw hex values or default Tailwind colours like `red-800`. Chart colours come from
`src/lib/theme.ts`, which mirrors the same tokens.

UI primitives are hand-rolled and headless (no Radix, no shadcn/ui): `src/components/ui`
(Button, Field/Input/Select/Textarea/Checkbox/Switch/Segmented, Tabs, Dropdown, Overlay, Badge,
Avatar, Skeleton, FileDrop, TagInput, RichTextEditor). Reuse them rather than writing new markup.

Every list view (Notifications, Staff, Admissions, Settings tables) must reuse the shared
`<DataTable />`; do not duplicate table markup per module.
Every destructive action must go through `<ConfirmDialog />`, and every create/update/delete must
raise a toast via `useToast()`.
Role gating goes through `<Can permission="…" />`, which reads `AuthContext`; permissions live in
`src/lib/permissions.ts`.

State: React Context for auth and toasts; Zustand stores in `src/store` for module data
(notifications, admissions, staff, settings). Do not introduce Redux.
Mock data lives in `src/data/*.ts`, typed by `src/types/*.ts`, and is always reached through the
thin service layer in `src/api/*.ts` so it can be swapped for real HTTP calls without touching
component props.
Zod schemas live in `src/validation/*.ts` and pair with react-hook-form.

Routing lives in `src/App.tsx` using `<Routes>`/`<Route>`, with `<ProtectedRoute />` wrapping
everything under `<DashboardLayout />` and `<ProtectedRoute adminOnly />` for admin-only routes.
Page components are lazy-loaded; keep new heavy pages lazy too.

Accessibility is not optional: every interactive element is keyboard reachable, uses
`focus-visible:ring-2 ring-wcbt-maroon`, and never places grey text on maroon.
